## 4. ARCHITECTURAL POSITIONING

Wendoro UI is the shared design system and reusable React component library for the Wendoro ecosystem.

Its responsibilities include:

- Brand identity and design tokens.
- Shared typography and spacing.
- Light, dark and system themes.
- Accessible reusable components.
- Layout and navigation primitives.
- Business-oriented UI components.
- Forms, feedback and data-display components.
- Shared styling and component documentation.
- External consumer compatibility.

It is intended to serve products such as:
- Wendoro Desk.
- Wendoro Flow.
- Wendoro Platform.
- Wendoro Studio.
- Wendoro Insights.
- Wendoro Support.
- Wendoro Commerce.
- Wendoro People.

Do not assume every product already exists or is production-ready.

### Critical separation of responsibilities

`@wendoro/ui` is a presentation library.

`@wendoro/sdk` is the Platform API client.

Product applications consume the UI library and the SDK as separate dependencies.

Do not:
- Add direct Platform API calls to UI components.
- Add database clients.
- Add Firebase initialization.
- Add product-specific backend business logic.
- Add tenant authorization logic to presentation components.
- Couple UI components to a specific backend.
- Add an unnecessary dependency on `@wendoro/sdk`.

The UI must support normal React application patterns and remain independently usable.

